  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-06-29T06:47:33.662Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "While attempting to build a multiplayer arcade cabinet, I ran into a somewhat unintuitive behaviour. \nSetting Ownership to another player in the same tick as updating a synced variable and requesting serialization causes a race. Sometimes the targeted player receives ownership *before* the latest synced variables. Other times they receive it *after* the latest Synced variables. This means that logic can be unpredictable / inconsistent, as the normally garaunteed manual sync becomes, well, less garaunteed. \nI am not sure if it is the intended behaviour, but if it is it should probably be spelled out in the docs at least (responding to or closing this would serve as documentation too! :) )\nIn the end I was able to work around the race condition by sending a playerId along with the rest of the synced data and using that in the OnDeserialized hook to set ownership with a garauntee of having the latest data, but this seems convoluted and unintuitive, so I'd prefer to see it patched so other folks don't spend a few hours pulling hair out.\nEither way, thanks for your time! <3",
